# Line endings are declared rather than left to the checkout, so a clone on a
# different machine cannot produce launchers that fail to run.
#
# The suite rule forces LF on shell scripts because a Windows checkout otherwise
# hands the container scripts it cannot execute. This project inverts for the
# same reason: cmd.exe parses a .cmd file line by line and LF-only endings break
# it in ways that look like a corrupt script rather than a checkout problem.

* text=auto

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf

*.png binary
